# shell: desktop
# mount: /devices/board1
# board: only
# A form a board's process publishes, drawn on the desktop and worked.
# The board ships no interface code: a process declares rows bound to
# its own storage, the desktop draws them, and a press writes the
# board's node, which the process hears as an event in its own thread.
# This needs a board on the cable, so it runs only with one.
wait 25
note the board's form opens itself, titled what the board called it
expect-title Board one
note and shows the board's own values
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/name workshop
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/status lamp off
note the toggle writes the board's node: the LED lights and the process,
note in its own thread, says so in its status row
click 480 234
wait 20
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/lamp 1
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/status lamp on
note and the panel's own status row is that text, live
expect-narrate lamp on
shot /tmp/trk_board_on.png
click 480 234
wait 20
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/lamp 0
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/status lamp off
note the button counts every press
click 560 290
wait 20
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/count 1
note the slider takes the value under the pointer, three quarters along
click 601 318
wait 20
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/bright 75
note the choice is pressed through its words, and the process hears it
click 560 346
wait 20
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/mode fast
note the entry takes the keyboard once clicked and writes on Return
click 560 262
wait 4
key h
key i
key Return
wait 20
expect-read /devices/board1/gui/demo/name workshophi
quit
